{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14576","id":4791237536,"node_id":"PR_kwDODUgI1s8AAAABHZR7oA","html_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14576","diff_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14576.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14576.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/issues/14576","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14576/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14576/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/issues/14576/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/statuses/d8cf808035b1d1e2052022c987d0e58545e3c609","number":14576,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"core: speed up workspace git checkouts, pulls and merges","user":{"login":"vito","id":1880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito","html_url":"https://github.com/vito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resuming a large agent session from a trace replays hundreds of workspace Git operations. Each one did far more work than its change needed: it re-fetched whole histories, rewrote whole worktrees and walked both whole trees to diff them. Builds on #14466.\n\n## Results\n\nCold resume of a recorded agent trace (dagger/dagger, engine built from source):\n\n| | Baseline | Previous best | This PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Wall time | 10m23s | 5m23s | **4m53s** |\n| Critical path (session client) | ~503s | ~233s | **~201s** |\n\nThese are single runs on different hosts, so read them as a trend. What's left on the critical path:\n- `GitRef.__fullCheckout`, 54s: mostly two cold remote checkouts and one fallback on shallow history.\n- Module loading, 42s.\n- The incoming side of native merges, 12s.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Fetch negotiation.** Workspace checkouts have a detached HEAD and no refs, so fetches into them re-received the whole history. They now negotiate from HEAD and the commits already joined.\n- **Copy-on-write full checkouts.** `GitRef.__fullCheckout` of a local ref builds on an existing checkout's snapshot instead of fetching into an empty repository. It writes only the tree delta, or checks the worktree out again in one pass when no ancestor checkout exists. Unusual repository layouts fall back to the fetch.\n- **Source trees** (`discardGitDir`) are built as deltas from any ancestor's tree, or from retained checkouts.\n- **Index refresh.** Retained checkouts' indexes have no stat data, so `reset --hard` and `restore .` rewrote every file. They now refresh the index first.\n- **Changeset merges.** The general merge stages only the scope of the changed paths, with the full base as a fallback. The native merge now handles new directories, directory metadata and empty directories, which were its last fallbacks to the general merge.\n- **`GitRef.tree` canonicalization.** Equivalent argument spellings are now one call and one snapshot, so diffs across them walk only the layers between them, not whole trees.\n- **Bundles** pack prerequisites and unbundle without holding the repository lock.\n- **`withReset`** checks that the target is reachable from HEAD, since copy-on-write checkouts can still hold orphaned commits.\n\n## Instrumentation\n\nEvery fast path records which path it took and why cheaper ones were skipped, as span attributes and wcprof markers (`git.checkout.delta[...]`, `git.tree.incremental[...]`, `git.native_merge.fallback[...]`). Merges profile each git command under its phase.\n\n## Testing\n\n`TestGit`, `TestChangeset` and the workspace commit, pull, reset and export tests pass. `TestWorkspaceCommitMergeBreakdown` (from #14466) now fails on any whole-tree changeset walk; it passes, with every merge taking the native path. Unit tests and lint pass.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-08T18:37:16Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T18:38:11Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T18:38:11Z","merged_at":"2026-10-09T18:38:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"1659c5690daa8c5c0d6ae8f428432a15b3411399","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"vito:workspace-git-perf","ref":"workspace-git-perf","repo":{"id":535736959,"node_id":"R_kgDOH-6yfw","name":"dagger","full_name":"vito/dagger","owner":{"login":"vito","id":1880,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4ODA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1880?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito","html_url":"https://github.com/vito","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vito/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","sit